So $20! < 3 \times 10^{18}$.
$21! = 21 \times 20! \approx 21 \times 2.43 \times 10^{18} \approx 51 \times 10^{18} = 5.1 \times 10^{19}$.
So indeed, $N$ will be at most 20.

Since the range of possible values for $N$ is very small (from 1 to 20), we can simply precompute the factorials or compute them on the fly and compare with $X$.
