The problem asks us to calculate the sum of $f(P)$ over all permutations $P$ of $(1, 2, \ldots, N)$, modulo 998244353.
$f(P)$ is formed by concatenating the decimal representations of the elements of $P$ and interpreting the result as an integer.

Let $P = (P_1, P_2, \ldots, P_N)$ be a permutation of $(1, 2, \ldots, N)$.
Let $L_i$ be the number of digits in the decimal representation of $i$.
Then $f(P)$ can be written as:
$f(P) = \sum_{i=1}^N P_i \cdot 10^{E_i}$
where $E_i$ is the number of digits contributed by elements $P_{i+1}, \ldots, P_N$.
Specifically, $E_i = \sum_{j=i+1}^N L_{P_j}$.
So, $f(P) = \sum_{i=1}^N P_i \cdot 10^{\sum_{j=i+1}^N L_{P_j}}$.

We need to compute $\sum_{P} f(P) \pmod{998244353}$.
By linearity of expectation (or just summation), this is equal to:
$\sum_{P} \sum_{i=1}^N P_i \cdot 10^{\sum_{j=i+1}^N L_{P_j}} = \sum_{i=1}^N \sum_{P} P_i \cdot 10^{\sum_{j=i+1}^N L_{P_j}}$.

Let's fix the position $i$ in the permutation. We want to sum $P_i \cdot 10^{\sum_{j=i+1}^N L_{P_j}}$ over all permutations $P$.
In a permutation $P$, the element at position $i$ can be any value $v \in \{1, \ldots, N\}$.
If $P_i = v$, then the remaining $N-1$ elements are a permutation of $\{1, \ldots, N\} \setminus \{v\}$.
The term $10^{\sum_{j=i+1}^N L_{P_j}}$ depends only on the set of values $\{P_{i+1}, \ldots, P_N\}$, which is $\{1, \ldots, N\} \setminus \{P_1, \ldots, P_i\}$.
Actually, the exponent depends on the values at positions $i+1, \ldots, N$.
Let $S_{i+1, N} = \{P_{i+1}, \ldots, P_N\}$. This is a subset of size $N-i$ from $\{1, \ldots, N\}$.
The contribution of a specific value $v$ at position $i$ is $v \cdot 10^{\sum_{u \in S_{i+1, N}} L_u}$.
For a fixed $v$ and a fixed subset $S_{i+1, N}$ such that $v \notin S_{i+1, N}$, how many permutations have $P_i = v$ and $\{P_{i+1}, \ldots, P_N\} = S_{i+1, N}$?
The elements $P_{i+1}, \ldots, P_N$ can be arranged in $(N-i)!$ ways. The elements $P_1, \ldots, P_{i-1}$ can be arranged in $(i-1)!$ ways.
So there are $(N-i)! (i-1)!$ such permutations.

Thus, the total sum is:
$\sum_{i=1}^N \sum_{v=1}^N v \cdot (N-i)! (i-1)! \sum_{S \subseteq \{1, \ldots, N\} \setminus \{v\}, |S|=N-i} 10^{\sum_{u \in S} L_u}$.

